{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<h1>Events</h1>
<p class="hint">Events happen on a day, or across a span of them.
  {{#suggestionsOn}}Anybody in the community can suggest one; somebody with the permission decides
  what goes on the calendar.{{/suggestionsOn}}
  {{^suggestionsOn}}Only people with the permission create them; everybody else answers.{{/suggestionsOn}}</p>
<div class="doing">
  <a class="btn" href="{{newUrl}}">{{{plusIcon}}}New event</a>
  {{#suggestionsOn}}<a class="btn secondary" href="{{suggestionsUrl}}">Suggested{{#anySuggested}} <span class="pill blue">{{openSuggestions}}</span>{{/anySuggested}}</a>{{/suggestionsOn}}
  <a class="btn secondary" href="{{calendarUrl}}">See what members see</a>
</div>
<details class="explain">
  <summary>Calendar invitations {{#invitesOn}}&mdash; on{{/invitesOn}}{{^invitesOn}}&mdash; not working{{/invitesOn}}</summary>
  {{^invitesOn}}<p class="problem">No invitation can be sent: {{invitesWhyNot}}.</p>{{/invitesOn}}
  {{#invitesOn}}
  <p>Pressing <strong>Invite everybody</strong> on an event sends a real calendar invitation to every
    approved member &mdash; the kind that appears in Gmail, Outlook and Apple Mail with accept, maybe
    and decline buttons on it. Whichever they press comes back to
    <code>{{replyTo}}</code> and lands on the guest list, without them opening this site at all.</p>
  <p class="hint">Sending is a button rather than something that happens when you save, for the same
    reason writing an invitation to a person is separate from sending it: an event whose day is
    still being argued about should not be in anybody's calendar yet. Changing an event afterwards
    marks it as needing a fresh invitation, and sending again is what moves it in everybody's
    calendar.</p>
  {{#remindOn}}<p class="hint">Anybody who has not answered is nudged <strong>{{remindDays}}</strong>
    day(s) before. Somebody who said no is never chased.</p>{{/remindOn}}
  {{^remindOn}}<p class="hint">Reminders are off. <code>calendar.remind-days-before</code> turns
    them back on.</p>{{/remindOn}}

  <h3>What the invitation says</h3>
  <p class="hint">The event's own words come first. This paragraph goes underneath, on every
    invitation &mdash; it is the part about the community rather than about the event, which is
    exactly the thing nobody wants to retype every time.
    {{#customTemplate}}This community has written its own.{{/customTemplate}}
    {{^customTemplate}}This is the wording that ships.{{/customTemplate}}
    Change it, and every other message this server sends, under
    <a href="{{messagesUrl}}">Messages</a>.</p>
  <blockquote class="preview">{{inviteTemplate}}</blockquote>
  {{/invitesOn}}
</details>
<div class="panel" data-panel="{{panelUrl}}">{{{panel}}}</div>
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
